{
  "dom_id": "question-166774",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Carmen cuts two pieces of drill fabric with lengths of $\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\text{m}$ and $\\frac{9}{7}\\,\\text{m}.$ The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\text{m}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $(\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7})\\text{m}.$\n\nTo add two fractions with unlike denominators, we need to express each fraction as an equivalent fraction with a common denominator.\n\nLet's look at the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7}\n$$\n\nThe least common denominator of $6$ and $7$ is $42.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{5}{6}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{5\\times 7}{6\\times 7}=\\frac{35}{42}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{9}{7}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}=\\frac{9\\times 6}{7\\times 6}=\\frac{54}{42}\n$$\n\nWe can now add the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we add the numerators.\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{42}+\\frac{54}{42}=\\frac{89}{42}\n$$\n\nExpressing this fraction as a mixed number, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{89}{42}=2\\,\\frac{5}{42}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $2\\,\\frac{5}{42}\\,\\text{m}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
